<section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
        <div class="head">
            <span class="eyebrow">What it does — and doesn't</span>
            <h2>A private reduction of the client's own exposure.</h2>
            <p class="lede">A senior cybersecurity expert reviews the client's own accounts, devices, apps, and access points in person, explains what matters in plain English, and reduces exposure where appropriate. The client stays present throughout. It does not investigate the other side, reconstruct past events, preserve chain of custody, collect evidence, or provide legal conclusions. It is not IT support and not a guarantee that no exposure remains.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
        <div class="head">
            <span class="eyebrow">How it works</span>
            <h2>Assessment first, then a reset if warranted.</h2>
            <p class="lede">Most clients begin with a Private Exposure Assessment — a paid, in-person diagnostic (&#8362;3,500, credited toward a full package within 14 days). If a full reset is warranted, it proceeds to Personal Shield or, for complex cases, Bespoke Private Protection. Full-package clients receive a private dated record and — only with the client's explicit authorization — an attorney-friendly summary describing the scope of work performed. It is not a forensic report, legal opinion, evidence document, or certification.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
    <div class="wrap cred">
        <div class="cred-lead">
            <span class="eyebrow">Safety-sensitive cases &amp; protocol</span>
            <h2>Timing, and how clients reach us.</h2>
            <p>In controlling-relationship situations, timing matters. The work follows the client's safety plan and your guidance; changes that could escalate danger are planned, not rushed. We coordinate with you only with the client's permission.</p>
        </div>
        <ul class="cred-list">
            <li>Initial contact is by WhatsApp or Signal, by the client.</li>
            <li>We ask clients not to send sensitive documents or detailed allegations in a first message.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
